text:
maria_product: Heads up — need final call on model discovery endpoint shape + capability flags before next planning sync. @aj_eng @sam_runtime please weigh in. TL;DR: customers asking for per-model tool list + streaming support + token caps.

aj_eng: Two proposals: minimal (top-level boolean flags + token_limit) vs rich (capabilities array with per-tool metadata). Minimal is faster to ship, rich is more future-proof.

sam_runtime: Runtime constraints: supporting per-request streaming + tool metadata increases payload size but OK. Main worry is compatibility across quantized variants and fallback behavior. Can we add an explicit fallback mapping?

lee_docs: Docs need a canonical example. Proposal for discovery response shape:
```json
{
  "model": "redwood-13b-v1",
  "capabilities_summary": {
    "streaming": true,
    "structured_output": true
  },
  "capabilities": [
    {
      "name": "streaming",
      "supported": true,
      "params": { "chunk_ms": 50 }
    },
    {
      "name": "tools",
      "supported": true,
      "tools": [
        {
          "id": "search",
          "display_name": "VectorSearch",
          "schema_url": "https://docs.redwood.ai/schemas/search-tool-v1.json"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "token_limit": 8192,
  "compatibility_profile": "redwood-13b-compat"
}
```

aj_eng: That looks good. Implementation note: keep a small top-level summary (capabilities_summary) so older SDKs can quickly decide without parsing arrays.

maria_product: Proposed launch criteria: 1) discovery endpoint stable for hosted + dedicated modes, 2) SDKs can parse capabilities_summary, 3) docs + migration guide published, 4) 2 pilot customers validate tooling metadata. Sound right?

ops-bot: deploy-bot: feature-flag "model-discovery-v1" toggled ON in staging at 1957772000 :white_check_mark:

sam_runtime: One ask from infra: include "compatibility_profile" string for fallback mapping (eg "llama-13b-8q" -> "llama-13b"). That reduces brittle client logic.

lee_docs: I'll draft examples, migration notes, and a quick snippet for SDKs. Small naming decision: use "supported" not "is_supported". Leaning to the shorter token.

aj_eng: Agree. We'll aim to implement the rich shape but expose the minimal summary for quick adopters. Plan to open PR for discovery endpoint + tests by EOD Thursday.

maria_product: Great — I'll add this to roadmap item "model discovery v1" and mark scope: MVP = summary + tools list + token_limit. Post-MVP: richer params + per-tool streaming hints. Thanks all :rocket:
